2. ~ the same: + #dependencies= and #development_dependencies=, the gems as words, in place of an add_dependency line apiece.
3. ~ the same: require_paths beside required_ruby_version, rather than after the files.
4. ~ the same: the gemspec first among the files.
5. ~ Browser::VERSION: /0.11.0/0.11.1/


## 20260907

0.11.0: + README.md

1. + README.md
2. ~ the Tor Browser caveat, corrected before it went in: it had said the library follows the install, where root_path is one fixed path.
3. It now says where the library looks, and that an install elsewhere wants bookmarks_location: and history_location:.
4. ~ browser.rb.gemspec: homepage, /browser.rb/browser/ and https, as http.rb's repository is http.
5. ~ README.md: the fork link, the same.
6. ~ Browser::VERSION: /0.10.1/0.11.0/


## 20260904

0.10.1: Ship String#ascii_only, so the gem loads without a RUBYLIB.

1. + lib/String/ascii_only.rb, required by Array#to_csv_row and resolved until now from ~/lib/ruby alone.
2. Requiring Browser::History therefore raised LoadError on any machine but the author's.
3. ~ Browser::VERSION: /0.10.0/0.10.1/


## 20260825

0.10.0: + Browser::Bookmark, the internal representation, and a lowercase load file.

1. + lib/Browser/Bookmark.rb: a bookmark which holds bookmarks; a folder has children, a leaf a url.
2. ~ Browser::Bookmarks.from_json, .from_plist, .from_sqlite: a Browser::Bookmark tree, in place of the raw parse.
3. ~ the same three: Chromium's and Safari's trees carry their folders.
4. ~ Browser::Bookmarks.from_plist: the History proxy skipped, and a leaf sitting at the top level taken.
5. ~ Browser::Bookmarks.from_sqlite: Firefox and Tor Browser flat still, the query fetching leaves alone.
6. ~ Browser::Bookmarks#to_objects: the tree flattened to title, url and folder, which the three renderers take.
7. ~ Browser::Bookmarks#to_csv: it had matched symbol keys against a string-keyed hash, so every row was empty commas.
8. - Browser::Bookmarks::Objects, which the flatten replaced.
9. - Browser::Bookmarks: require 'Array/to_csv_row', which nothing there used.
10. /lib/Browser.rb/lib/browser.rb/, /test/Browser_test.rb/test/browser_test.rb/, require 'Browser' --> require 'browser'.
11. The uppercase name folded together with the browser gem on a case-insensitive filesystem.
12. ~ lib/browser.rb: - the header's version and Changes block, VERSION.rb and this CHANGELOG being the one of each.
13. + test/Browser/Bookmark_test.rb
14. ~ test/Browser/*_test.rb: #bookmarks checked through to_objects, in place of a raw round-trip.
15. ~ Browser::VERSION: /0.9.0/0.10.0/


## 20260823

